WEBVTT

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:21.160
The temperature will increase over the morning due to a migratory anticyclone, which leaves us with a nice calm day.

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.380
The nice weather will continue throughout the weekend.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:28.210
Good morning, Mom!

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:31.840
Why did you wake up so late, Cindy?

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.010
It's such a nice day today.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.050
It is!

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:39.260
We can even see to the mountains!

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:44.390
Even though I cannot see the mountains, I can smell that today is different.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:49.730
Today's what you would call an <i>Indian Summer</i> isn't it?

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.240
<i>Indian Summer</i>  eh?

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.490
Your poor late father used to sing a song called that.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.580
Anyway...

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.750
Has Hank called you since last time?

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:06.580
No phone calls...

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:11.750
If he left Reno last night, then he should be here any time now.

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:15.010
I guess that's right...

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:21.010
A car is coming!

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.440
Hank! Is it Hank?

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.650
It's not my brother. It's a customer.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:35.990
I see.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:38.110
Welcome!

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.280
Do you have anything to eat?

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:48.000
We have some roast beef sandwiches, potato salad... and some eggs!

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:49.630
That will do.

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:56.130
It's really early. Have you been driving all night?

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:21.320
I held my breath and kept waiting while my heart was scratched away

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:32.670
A minute, a second never felt so long

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:44.430
I look up at the sky and ask the wind, "Can I fly now?"

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.730
The weak person I was is no more

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:56.320
I decided to just believe

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:03.450
With the dreams I once had in my hand now

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:07.290
I go towards you

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:15.000
Carrying those emotions I felt when I broke

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.130
I go towards you

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.180
Blown by the wind

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:28.640
Oh blown

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:35.270
Indian Summer

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:40.530
Did you enjoy your meal?

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:41.110
Yeah.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.320
It was good.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.370
My mother's gravy is the best isn't it?

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.750
She may not be able to see, but mom's nose and tongue are the best in the world!

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.330
This restaurant used to be a thriving business until two years ago.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:04:00.340
Then a new hotel opened up, and all the customers left.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:04.340
I want to take a nap. Do you have a room?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.680
It's $25 a day.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:12.350
Go up the stairs, and at the end is room eight.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:14.850
Do you want me to wake you up?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:16.650
No, thank you.

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:45.510
Sheriff. You're early today.

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:48.600
Hi, Mercer.

00:04:49.220 --> 00:04:51.850
It sure is early today.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:54.230
Has something happened?

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:57.480
A robbery at a casino in Reno.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:58.610
Robbery?

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:03.240
They robbed the winnings and killed two guards in the getaway.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.110
They're said to have fled out here.

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.740
That's rather disturbing.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.250
There's a real nice car parked here...

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:15.500
Tt's a customer. I reckon he's not from around here.

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:20.250
The way he walked was calm however; he doesn't seem to be fleeing from anyone.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.800
As perceptive as ever I see.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.720
Californian plates, and the muffler is still warm.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.470
Do you want an ID check?

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:32.270
No need. Meeting him will save us the trouble.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:34.310
Morning Cindy!

00:05:34.810 --> 00:05:35.890
Morning!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.650
I heard what you said. A robbery?

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:40.900
Yeah.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.150
They've taken to this area... are you sure?

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.240
Nothing is certain.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:48.740
Who's the recent customer?

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:51.740
Really? Him?

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.830
I didn't mean it's him.

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:57.790
I'm just curious about his character.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.140
I'd like some ice water.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:17.770
I'm so sorry! I forgot to tell you the ice machine is out of order.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.070
You're traveling?

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:24.440
Right.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.070
Where to?

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:29.570
Salt Lake City.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:33.700
Oh, I see. That's why you're taking a break.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.040
Here you go!

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:38.830
Thank you.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.340
Well, it's time for us to get going.

00:06:48.670 --> 00:06:52.180
Thanks Cindy. We'll come again for dinner some time.

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:55.010
By then my brother should have returned!

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.390
Hank?

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.100
Yep!

00:06:57.480 --> 00:07:01.230
Come to think of it, he's been working at a farm in California.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:04.650
It's almost time for the end of the migrant worker season.

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.280
There was a phone call from Reno last night.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:10.030
He said he'd be back after he made a lot of noise.

00:07:10.450 --> 00:07:11.450
Reno, eh?

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:14.280
I hope the gamblers haven't fleeced him of his wages.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.910
My brother will be fine...

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:20.290
He earned that money in order to rebuild this place after all.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.500
I know, it was a joke.

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:28.300
When it comes to Hank, he'll quit after losing five dollars to the slots.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:32.010
Sheriff.

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:33.090
What is it?

00:07:33.890 --> 00:07:34.760
it's him.

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:39.180
Anyone with eyes that sharp can't be just a tourist.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.730
Either way, it's better to check him out.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:44.730
Didn't you hear the radio?

00:07:45.150 --> 00:07:49.070
Both suspects are reported to be young white males.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:50.780
Ah, that's right.

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:51.820
Sorry.

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.080
Is Hank coming back?

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:57.200
Yup.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.450
That's real nice.

00:07:59.080 --> 00:08:06.090
I have been regretting making him leave his home here for work.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.590
Well, he'll come back nice and cheerful!

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:09.920
See you later!

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:27.190
The couple of armed robbers who attacked the hotel/casino Richland in Reno city last night made off with approximately 800,000 dollars.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:33.780
They killed two guards in their getaway. There is no word of their whereabouts.

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:42.910
Reno city police will be aided by the FBI.  A suspect has been named as Ted Coleman, 28, from Chicago.  The police are still in pursuit of the suspects.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.260
Is that Hank?

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:03.270
Yeah, it's me, Mom!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.770
Hank!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:05.440
Mom!

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:10.400
How have you been, Hank?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:12.230
Ah, I'm great!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:14.650
I feel so good I could fly!

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:21.370
I was worried that the farm work would be too hard for you!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:25.370
Nonsense! It's just like the picnics we used to go on.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.630
Brother! Welcome home!

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.930
Yo Cindy! I'm home!

00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.640
Well look at you, big and strong now!

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.640
Well, aren't you hungry then?

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:48.520
I just ate a tasteless hamburger, so I'm fine for now.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:52.530
Hank, did you bring a friend with you?

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:55.400
Er, nobody else.

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:57.200
Right Cindy?

00:09:57.660 --> 00:09:58.410
Nope.

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:01.530
Anyway, I'm going to take a nap. I'm beat.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.040
The rooms are empty right?

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:09.210
Right, all but number eight.

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.460
Eight? Oh I see.

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:14.210
The parked car is a customer's?

00:10:14.760 --> 00:10:18.930
Yup. The only room that locks anymore is eight.

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:20.890
I understand Cindy.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.560
Now that I'm back, I can completely renovate this place!

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:26.270
Really, brother?

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:30.600
Yessir! We'll put a piano here, and a jukebox here!

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.020
We'll bring this place back together!

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:38.030
Well Mom, I'll tell you my stories later. Now I need to take a nap.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:01.680
It's just you.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:03.800
Amazing!

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.810
It's just as the radio says. Exactly 800,000 dollars.

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.520
This is your share. 200,000 dollars.

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:12.810
R-right..

00:11:13.310 --> 00:11:15.400
This is my 200,000 share.

00:11:16.070 --> 00:11:18.820
And this is 400,000 dollars for the boss.

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:21.780
What are you going to do, Ted?

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.830
After I give the money to the boss, I'll skip town.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.830
Skipping town... are you ok?

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:31.080
Aren't you worried?

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.120
What?

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:36.920
The casino we attacked belongs to the Nevada family’s Don.

00:11:37.460 --> 00:11:39.720
Willy Dicarno's place!

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:45.010
Don't worry. Our boss can deal with it.

00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:48.560
It was his plan after all.

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:52.020
But we killed two guards!

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:56.820
They were mafia men. Killing them was not part of the plan.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:01.740
They know who you are! You think the boss can still help you?

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.320
Things will work out.

00:12:04.320 --> 00:12:07.530
Anyway, your family doesn't suspect you right?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:13.120
Don’t worry.  Like I told you before, my mother can't see. My sister didn't notice either.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.050
Besides, in this town I pass for a nice boy.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:19.130
Heh, a good boy.

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:23.630
Still, the mafia worries me.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.140
Hank...

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:28.430
They say their network is national.

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:36.770
They say the taxi driver, the hotel doorman, even the police are all their informants.

00:12:37.150 --> 00:12:39.150
It will be easy for them to find us.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:44.910
Shut up! I don't need to listen to this talk. I'm taking a nap.

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:47.450
Ted...

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.370
Hank...

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:59.920
If I do get arrested, I will never say your name. Relax.

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:06.340
I'd just say I met some nameless guy at a farm.

00:13:08.050 --> 00:13:08.930
Ted...

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:10.510
Goodnight.

00:13:52.770 --> 00:13:56.140
Well, gotta make some distance before sunset.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:00.230
The weather's really nice. Should be a comfortable drive.

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:05.030
Yeah, if only I could be playing golf today; it would be even better!

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:07.150
Thanks girlie, it was tasty.

00:14:07.860 --> 00:14:09.870
Thanks! Please come again!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:14.410
Ah, Brother. Did you sleep well?

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.500
Yeah, but I'm so hungry it woke me up!

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:23.090
I can whip you up a ham sandwich, cheeseburger and some mashed potatoes if you like.

00:14:23.090 --> 00:14:26.630
That sounds good. Make sure to pour lots of gravy!

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:29.640
As expected, you really missed Mom's home cooked meals eh?

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:31.890
Yup. Can you make two servings?

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.270
Two servings? You can eat that much?

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:39.270
I told you I'm starving! Just do it.

00:14:40.400 --> 00:14:41.150
Okay.

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:42.230
By the way...

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.860
The customers in room eight...

00:14:46.610 --> 00:14:47.780
What kind of people are they?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.320
They... It's just one guy.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.790
One? He is with a woman isn't he?

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.500
Alone. He said he was traveling.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:01.790
He arrived here an hour before you got back. Said he wanted to take a nap.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:05.300
Why, what's wrong?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:09.800
Tell me what he looks like. Anything. Just tell me what you saw.

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:14.680
Probably Asian, but with a massive body...

00:15:15.600 --> 00:15:19.140
He's probably a karate or judo teacher.

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.600
His stare startled me when I first saw him.

00:15:22.060 --> 00:15:23.310
He looks like a hitman, doesn't he?

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.610
Hitman? No way!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:27.820
Why do you ask?

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:34.070
Oh, I just happened to hear there was a mafia hitman in the area.

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.120
I was a little worried.

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.120
He could be a killer.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.830
Possibly.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:41.000
Mom!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:45.460
He is not normal, I can feel it.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:49.800
Hank, tell me you are not involved with him at all.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.800
Wh.. What are you talking about Mom?

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.010
There's no way I'm involved with him.

00:15:55.010 --> 00:15:58.060
Can I believe you, Hank?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.350
O.. of course!

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.070
Oh, are you leaving already?

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:14.950
Yes.

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.130
He doesn't look normal at all.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:28.460
Could be Asian... Who in the world is he?

00:16:37.260 --> 00:16:41.480
Although I cannot see him, he smells like a beast.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:42.390
A beast?

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:45.690
Yes. He breathes like a puma.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:50.070
B.. but he's gone! He left, right?

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.080
I almost jumped him.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.050
I saw a hitman with those eyes on TV.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:15.630
Ok then. I'm out of here.

00:17:24.390 --> 00:17:25.310
Mom!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.230
Hank!

00:17:26.690 --> 00:17:31.320
I know that there is another man in this room!

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:33.860
What are you saying, Mom?

00:17:34.440 --> 00:17:35.740
No one is here.

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:43.950
Hank! Where is the man who enticed you into robbing the casino? Where!

00:17:43.950 --> 00:17:44.710
Mom!

00:17:44.710 --> 00:17:49.330
You roped my precious son into a life of vice.

00:17:49.880 --> 00:17:51.710
I will never forgive this!

00:17:51.710 --> 00:17:54.880
I will kill him with your father's gun!

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:59.890
Mom, please stay calm. You can't use a gun!

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.430
Hank, push him to me - where is the guy?

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:07.480
S.. STOP!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:21.580
Hank?

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:23.370
Hank?

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:26.200
Hank?!

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:35.340
Hank...

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:38.800
Is he dead, Hank?

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:46.600
He's dead, Mom.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:48.310
Really?

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:50.520
Is he really dead?

00:18:51.440 --> 00:18:54.570
Really, it's ok now.

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:58.700
Hank, where is Hank?

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:02.120
He said he was going far away, then he left.

00:19:05.200 --> 00:19:06.080
Hank...

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:07.620
Hank...

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:09.410
Hank...

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:20.590
Concerning last night's attack at the casino in Reno,

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:23.850
Suspect Ted Coleman, age 28, and another unidentified person are still at large.

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:27.470
No word on their current known location.

00:19:30.310 --> 00:19:30.730
Hank...

00:19:31.940 --> 00:19:34.150
You were out of luck.

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.000
Sorry for being late.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.210
There were a few inconveniences.

00:19:56.670 --> 00:20:00.170
Seems like you had too many inconveniences.

00:20:01.130 --> 00:20:03.760
Your identity's been revealed.

00:20:05.510 --> 00:20:07.140
What are you going to do, Ted?

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.690
I'll fly out quick and not cause you any trouble.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:12.890
Useless!

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:15.110
They know who you are.

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:19.150
Wait, I can get away without trouble!

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.490
Shit.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.580
You want to keep all the money!

00:20:59.940 --> 00:21:02.240
Are you Willy Dicarno's hitman?

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:06.620
I see...

00:21:07.070 --> 00:21:11.240
Dicarno suspected that it wasn't just Hank and Ted.

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.790
He cut them some slack, and it led right to me.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:25.550
You disappointed that the big job was planned by a lowly county sheriff?

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:33.270
Well, don't think I'm easy just because I'm a sheriff.

00:21:33.770 --> 00:21:36.140
My quickdraw is the fastest in Utah.

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:39.650
I won the contest four years ago.

00:22:33.870 --> 00:22:39.120
It doesn't matter anymore

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:44.670
Who craved freedom first

00:22:45.840 --> 00:22:53.560
How we decided to part, and how we loved each other

00:22:53.850 --> 00:22:55.890
As nostalgic and simply just that

00:22:55.890 --> 00:23:03.980
Once you've lost it you'll feel lonely

00:23:04.230 --> 00:23:07.900
You may have to overcome the pain

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:13.160
Many times with that cruel heart of yours

00:23:13.200 --> 00:23:21.370
But you just can't become as strong as you've imagined

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.960
It was just a dream

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:29.380
So let us return to tomorrow

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:34.390
In this calm night

00:23:34.430 --> 00:23:36.640
There'll only be wanderers

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:41.770
But now you've awakened, so walk down that path of yours

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:47.730
And even though time is fleeting

00:23:47.780 --> 00:23:54.200
People sometimes desire too much

00:24:01.790 --> 00:24:05.880
By chance, Golgo's plane is hijacked!

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:11.130
The criminals take the passengers hostage with reckless demands!

00:24:12.340 --> 00:24:18.470
Which intelligence service entrusted him with the code "Psalm #13"?

00:24:19.100 --> 00:24:20.430
Just one word.

00:24:20.810 --> 00:24:25.980
Jet Stream

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:22.520
Next time, on Gorgon 13:

00:24:23.020 --> 00:24:24.520
Jet Stream

00:24:25.360 --> 00:24:28.780
Don't stand behind him if you value your life.
